  <h1>🥗 Diet Tracking</h1>

  <h3>🍎 1. Why Diet Tracking Is Important</h3>
  <p>“You can’t improve what you don’t track.” Diet tracking helps you become aware of your eating habits, portion sizes, and nutrient intake.</p>

  <h3>📲 2. How to Track Your Diet</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Use apps like MyFitnessPal, LoseIt, or Yazio</li>
    <li>Record every meal/snack immediately</li>
    <li>Include beverages, sauces, and hidden calories</li>
    <li>Review weekly calorie and nutrient summary</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>🥦 3. Balanced Nutrition Checklist</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Protein: lean meats, beans, tofu, eggs</li>
    <li>Carbs: whole grains, fruits, vegetables</li>
    <li>Fats: nuts, seeds, olive oil</li>
    <li>Hydration: at least 2–3L of water daily</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>🕗 4. Meal Planning Tips</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Prep meals in advance to avoid impulse eating</li>
    <li>Follow the “80/20 rule” – 80% nutritious food, 20% treats</li>
    <li>Eat slowly and mindfully</li>
    <li>Don’t skip breakfast</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>🌼 5. Signs of a Healthy Diet</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Steady energy levels throughout the day</li>
    <li>Good digestion</li>
    <li>Clearer skin and better mood</li>
    <li>Stable weight</li>
  </ul>

